Woodpecker CI on FenrirOS
=========================

Installed inert: neither service is enabled, and the settings files
(/etc/woodpecker/server.env, agent.env) are empty.

    1. Register an OAuth application in your forge (Gitea or Forgejo:
       Settings, Applications) with the redirect URI
       https://<ci host>/authorize.
    2. Fill /etc/woodpecker/server.env from
       /usr/share/doc/woodpecker/server.env.example (host, a fresh agent
       secret, the forge and its client id and secret, WOODPECKER_ADMIN).
    3. dinitctl enable woodpecker-server
       The server listens on 127.0.0.1:8000 (HTTP, put a reverse proxy with
       TLS in front) and on :9000 for the agents (gRPC; firewall it or bind
       it to a private address with WOODPECKER_GRPC_ADDR).
    4. Fill /etc/woodpecker/agent.env (same agent secret) and
       dinitctl enable woodpecker-agent. For the docker backend add the
       woodpecker-agent user to the docker group (moby package): doing so
       lets CI jobs control the host's containers, so run agents on a
       machine you accept that for.

woodpecker-cli is the command line client (WOODPECKER_SERVER and
WOODPECKER_TOKEN from your user page).
